  "//autoTerms": "MACHINE-SET, not Tina's \u2014 but LOOKED AT, not guessed. Every one of these 890 colourway names was read off a real product photograph on a contact sheet (scripts/colour-sheets.mjs builds them, 30 names per sheet). That replaced three automated attempts that were all measured and all worse: a pixel sampler at 45%, zero-shot CLIP at 74%, and a probe trained on a HuggingFace fashion dataset at 48.5%. Tina, 2026-08-29: \"i just dont get how you cant look at the pictures.\" She was right. A null here means the name is not a colour at all \u2014 a garment (\"jilbab\", \"trench coat\"), a fabric (\"viscose blend\", \"muslin\"), a size or a product code (\"w25218\") \u2014 which is the judgement no automated reader made correctly, because asked what colour a garment is it always answers with one. lib/colour.ts consults this ONLY where `terms` above has no entry, so answering a term in the review page permanently overrules it. Rebuild the sheets with: npx tsx scripts/colour-sheets.mjs",
